location-daemon on FreeBSD: the gpsd it started for its clients stops
again when they are gone. location-daemon ends 15 s after the last
client has let go of liblocation's lock, but it never stopped the gpsd
it had started: on the Pro1X gpsd, pro1x-gnss and the modem's GNSS
engine behind them then ran until the next boot after the first app
that asked for a position (rc.d/pro1x_gps, freebsd/modem/README.md
stage 3). Stopped the way it was started: the start hook's "stop"
(location-daemon-gpsd, which keeps a gpsd started at boot by
pro1x_gps_enable="YES"), else gpsd's rc.d script. A gpsd that ran
before location-daemon came is left alone.

As in the upstream fix (maemo-leste/location-daemon#1): gps_close()
first, then the stop, and both before the D-Bus name is released, so a
client starting right then can't activate a new instance onto the gpsd
being stopped.

diff --git a/location-daemon.c b/location-daemon.c
index 2d7bc08..3e97292 100644
--- a/location-daemon.c
+++ b/location-daemon.c
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@ static GThread *poll_thread;
 static DBusConnection *dbus;
 static struct gps_data_t gpsdata;
 static int running = 0;
+static int started_gpsd = 0;
 
 int sighandler(gpointer sig)
 {
@@ -316,6 +317,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 		switch (system(access(GPSD_START_HOOK, X_OK) == 0 ?
 		    GPSD_START_HOOK " start" : "/usr/sbin/service gpsd onestart")) {
 		case 0:
+			started_gpsd = 1;
 			/* Give time to settle */
 			sleep(1);
 			break;
@@ -354,15 +356,19 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 
 	dbus_send_va(RUNNING_INTERFACE, "Running", DBUS_TYPE_BYTE, &running, DBUS_TYPE_INVALID);
 
+	(void)gps_stream(&gpsdata, WATCH_DISABLE, NULL);
+	(void)gps_close(&gpsdata);
+
+	if (started_gpsd && system(access(GPSD_START_HOOK, X_OK) == 0 ?
+	    GPSD_START_HOOK " stop" : "/usr/sbin/service gpsd onestop") != 0)
+		g_warning("unable to stop gpsd");
+
 	if (dbus_bus_release_name(dbus, DAEMON_DBUS_NAME, NULL) == -1) {
 		g_critical("Cannot release DBUS name");
 	}
 	dbus_connection_close(dbus);
 	dbus_connection_unref(dbus);
 
-	(void)gps_stream(&gpsdata, WATCH_DISABLE, NULL);
-	(void)gps_close(&gpsdata);
-
 	g_main_loop_unref(mainloop);
 
 	return 0;
